ue}},\"_meta\":{\"_isLoaded\":true}},\"cover_image\":{\"attribution\":\"Stephan\",\"attribution_url\":\"https://www.komoot.de/user/207373672394\",\"src\":\"https://d2exd72xrrp1s7.cloudfront.net/www/collection/797/1G46fP?width=%7Bwidth%7D&height=%7Bheight%7D&crop=%7Bcrop%7D\",\"type\":\"image/*\",\"_links\":{\"self\":{\"href\":\"https://api.komoot.de/v007/collections/797/cover_image\"}},\"_meta\":{\"_isLoaded\":true}},\"share_urls\":{\"share_urls\":{\"de\":\"https://www.komoot.com/de-de/collection/797/der-nordseekuesten-radweg-teil-7-schottland\",\"en\":\"https://www.komoot.com/collection/797/the-north-sea-coast-cycle-route-part-7-scotland\",\"fr\":\"https://www.komoot.com/fr-fr/collection/797/la-north-sea-coast-cycle-route-partie-7-scotland\",\"it\":\"https://www.komoot.com/it-it/collection/797/il-percorso-ciclabile-della-costa-del-mare-del-nord-parte-7-scozia\",\"nl\":\"https://www.komoot.com/nl-nl/collection/797/de-north-sea-coast-cycle-route-deel-7-scotland\",\"es\":\"https://www.komoot.com/es-es/collection/797/la-ruta-ciclista-de-la-costa-del-mar-del-norte-parte-7-escocia\"},\"_links\":{},\"_meta\":{\"_isLoaded\":true}}}},{\"id\":3596813,\"type\":\"GUIDE\",\"name\":\"Easy hikes around Ettrick And Yarrow\",\"region_name\":\"Ettrick And Yarrow\",\"region_name_with_prep\":\"around Ettrick And Yarrow\",\"region_id\":163434,\"region_type\":\"town-city\",\"sport\":\"hike\",\"intro\":\"&amp;lt;div class=\\\"guide-intro\\\"&amp;gt;\\n  &amp;lt;p class=\\\"intro-overview\\\"&amp;gt;\\n    Easy hiking trails around Ettrick And Yarrow traverse a landscape characterized by delightful river valleys, glistening lochs, and extensive woodlands, set against a backdrop of majestic hills and wild moorland. The region is shaped by the Ettrick Water and Yarrow Water, tributaries of the River Tweed, offering pleasant walking routes along their banks. St Mary's Loch, the largest natural lake in the Scottish Borders, and the picturesque Loch of the Lowes are prominent water features. This diverse terrain provides a scenic setting for outdoor pursuits.\\n  &amp;lt;/p&amp;gt;\\n\\n  &amp;lt;h2&amp;gt;Best easy hiking trails around Ettrick And Yarrow&amp;lt;/h2&amp;gt;\\n  &amp;lt;ul class=\\\"trail-highlights\\\"&amp;gt;\\n    &amp;lt;li&amp;gt;\\n      The most popular easy hiking route is &amp;lt;a href=\\\"https://www.komoot.com/smarttour/e1294111217/cottage-wood-and-haining-loch-loop-from-selkirk-roxburghshire\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener\\\"&amp;gt;Cottage Wood and Haining Loch loop from Selkirk — Roxburghshire&amp;lt;/a&amp;gt;, a 3.2 miles (5.2 km) trail that takes 1 hour 23 minutes to complete. This loop offers gentle gradients around a tranquil loch and through peaceful woodlands.\\n    &amp;lt;/li&amp;gt;\\n\\n    &amp;lt;li&amp;gt;\\n      Another top favourite among local hikers is &amp;lt;a href=\\\"https://www.komoot.com/smarttour/e1294473914/hare-moss-and-big-wood-loop-from-dunhog-moss\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener\\\"&amp;gt;Hare Moss and Big Wood loop from Dunhog Moss&amp;lt;/a&amp;gt;, an easy 4.6 miles (7.4 km) path. This route winds through open mossland and mature forest, providing varied scenery.\\n    &amp;lt;/li&amp;gt;\\n\\n    &amp;lt;li&amp;gt;\\n      Local hikers also love the &amp;lt;a href=\\\"https://www.komoot.com/smarttour/e1294104053/selkirk-bridge-and-linglie-bridge-loop-from-victoria-park-roxburghshire\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener\\\"&amp;gt;Selkirk Bridge and Linglie Bridge loop from Victoria Park — Roxburghshire&amp;lt;/a&amp;gt;, a 2.7 miles (4.3 km) trail leading through river valleys, often completed in about 1 hour 6 minutes.\\n    &amp;lt;/li&amp;gt;\\n\\n    &amp;lt;li&amp;gt;\\n      Hiking around Ettrick And Yarrow is defined by lush river valleys, expansive lochs, and ancient woodlands. The network offers options for various easy hiking trails suitable for different ability levels.\\n    &amp;lt;/li&amp;gt;\\n\\n    &amp;lt;li&amp;gt;\\n      The routes in Ettrick And Yarrow are highly rated by the komoot community with an average score of 4.5 stars from over 300 reviews. More than 3,600 hikers have used komoot to explore Ettrick And Yarrow's varied terrain.\\n    &amp;lt;/li&amp;gt;\\n  &amp;lt;/ul&amp;gt;\\n&amp;lt;/div&amp;gt;\",\"sanitized_intro\":[\"Easy hiking trails around Ettrick And Yarrow traverse a landscape characterized by delightful river valleys, glistening lochs, and extensive woodlands, set against a backdrop of majestic hills and wild moorland. The region is shaped by the Ettrick Water and Yarrow Water, tributaries of the River Tweed, offering pleasant walking routes along their banks. St Mary&#39;s Loch, the largest natural lake in the Scottish Borders, and the picturesque Loch of the Lowes are prominent water features. This diverse terrain provides a scenic setting for outdoor pursuits.\",\"Best easy hiking trails around Ettrick And Yarrow\",\"The most popular easy hiking route is Cottage Wood and Haining Loch loop from Selkirk — Roxburghshire, a 3.2 miles (5.2 km) trail that takes 1 hour 23 minutes to complete. This loop offers gentle gradients around a tranquil loch and through peaceful woodlands.\",\"Another top favourite among local hikers is Hare Moss and Big Wood loop from Dunhog Moss, an easy 4.6 miles (7.4 km) path. This route winds through open mossland and mature forest, providing varied scenery.\",\"Local hikers also love the Selkirk Bridge and Linglie Bridge loop from Victoria Park — Roxburghshire, a 2.7 miles (4.3 km) trail leading through river valleys, often completed in about 1 hour 6 minutes.\",\"Hiking around Ettrick And Yarrow is defined by lush river valleys, expansive lochs, and ancient woodlands. The network offers options for various easy hiking trails suitable for different ability levels.\",\"The routes in Ettrick And Yarrow are highly rated by the komoot community with an average score of 4.5 stars from over 300 reviews. More than 3,600 hikers have used komoot to explore Ettrick And Yarrow&#39;s varied terrain.\"],\"intro_plain\":\"Easy hiking trails around Ettrick And Yarrow traverse a landscape characterized by delightful river valleys, glistening lochs, and extensive woodlands, set against a backdrop of majestic hills and wild moorland. The region is shaped by the Ettrick Water and Yarrow Water, tributaries of the River Tweed, offering pleasant walking routes along their banks. St Mary's Loch, the largest natural lake in the Scottish Borders, and the picturesque Loch of the Lowes are prominent water features. This diverse terrain provides a scenic setting for outdoor pursuits. Best easy hiking trails around Ettrick And Yarrow The most popular easy hiking route is Cottage Wood and Haining Loch loop from Selkirk — Roxburghshire, a 3.2 miles (5.2 km) trail that takes 1 hour 23 minutes to complete. This loop offers gentle gradients around a tranquil loch and through peaceful woodlands. Another top favourite among local hikers is Hare Moss and Big Wood loop from Dunhog Moss, an easy 4.6 miles (7.4 km) path. This route winds through open mossland and mature forest, providing varied scenery. Local hikers also love the Selkirk Bridge and Linglie Bridge loop from Victoria Park — Roxburghshire, a 2.7 miles (4.3 km) trail leading through river valleys, often completed in about 1 hour 6 minutes. Hiking around Ettrick And Yarrow is defined by lush river valleys, expansive lochs, and ancient woodlands. The network offers options for various easy hiking trails suitable for different ability levels. The routes in Ettrick And Yarrow are highly rated by the komoot community with an average score of 4.5 stars from over 300 reviews. More than 3,600 hikers have used komoot to explore Ettrick And Yarrow's varied terrain.\",\"faq\":[{\"question\":\"How many easy hiking trails are available in Ettrick And Yarrow?\",\"answer\":\"Ettrick And Yarrow offers a wide selection of easy hiking trails, with over 80 routes specifically categorized as easy. In total, the region features more than 240 hiking routes for various ability levels.\"},{\"question\":\"What kind of terrain can I expect on easy hikes in Ettrick And Yarrow?\",\"answer\":\"Easy hikes in Ettrick And Yarrow typically traverse delightful river valleys, glistening lochs, and extensive woodlands. You'll find paths along the banks of the Ettrick Water and Yarrow Water, as well as routes through open mossland and mature forests, offering varied and scenic backdrops.\"},{\"question\":\"Are there any family-friendly easy walks in the area?\",\"answer\":\"Yes, many easy trails in Ettrick And Yarrow are suitable for families. For example, the &amp;lt;a href=\\\"https://www.komoot.com/smarttour/e1294111217/cottage-wood-and-haining-loch-loop-from-selkirk-roxburghshire\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener\\\"&amp;gt;Cottage Wood and Haining Loch loop from Selkirk&amp;lt;/a&amp;gt; is a gentle 5.2 km route around a tranquil loch and through peaceful woodlands, ideal for a family outing. Bowhill Country Estate also offers leisurely options like \\\"The Lochs Walk\\\" and \\\"The Lady's Walk\\\" with family-friendly attractions nearby.\"},{\"question\":\"Can I bring my dog on the easy hiking trails?\",\"answer\":\"Many trails in Ettrick And Yarrow are dog-friendly, allowing you to enjoy the scenic beauty with your canine companion. It's always recommended to keep dogs on a lead, especially near livestock or in nature conservation areas, and to check specific route details for any restrictions. The varied landscapes of river valleys and woodlands provide excellent opportunities for walks with your dog.\"},{\"question\":\"What historical landmarks or points of interest can I see on easy hikes?\",\"answer\":\"The region is rich in history. You can explore medieval Tower Houses such as Newark Tower, Blackhouse Tower, Dryhope Tower, and Kirkhope Tower. The &amp;lt;a href=\\\"https://www.komoot.com/smarttour/19081135\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener\\\"&amp;gt;Newark Castle Ruins loop from Bowhill House&amp;lt;/a&amp;gt; is an easy 5 km hike that takes you past the impressive &amp;lt;a href=\\\"https://www.komoot.com/highlight/6144513\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener\\\"&amp;gt;Newark Castle Ruins&amp;lt;/a&amp;gt;. Other highlights include ancient standing stones and Bronze Age settlements scattered throughout the valleys.\"},{\"question\":\"Are there any waterfalls accessible on easy trails?\",\"answer\":\"While some of the more dramatic waterfalls like the &amp;lt;a href=\\\"https://www.komoot.com/highlight/4924314\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener\\\"&amp;gt;Grey Mare’s Tail Waterfall&amp;lt;/a&amp;gt; might involve more challenging terrain, the region does feature several beautiful waterfalls. You can explore areas like &amp;lt;a href=\\\"https://www.komoot.com/highlight/4568103\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener\\\"&amp;gt;Craigmechan Scar Gorge and Waterfall&amp;lt;/a&amp;gt; or &amp;lt;a href=\\\"https://www.komoot.com/highlight/6114857\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener\\\"&amp;gt;Wolfcleugh Waterfall&amp;lt;/a&amp;gt;, though accessibility on easy trails may vary. Always check the specific route details for difficulty.\"},{\"question\":\"What is the best time of year to go hiking in Ettrick And Yarrow?\",\"answer\":\"Ettrick And Yarrow offers beautiful hiking opportunities year-round. Spring brings lush greenery and blooming wildflowers, while autumn showcases vibrant foliage. Summer provides longer daylight hours and generally pleasant weather. Even in winter, the tranquil landscapes can be stunning, though some paths might be muddy or icy, so appropriate gear is essential.\"},{\"question\":\"Are there any circular easy walks in Ettrick And Yarrow?\",\"answer\":\"Yes, the region is well-known for its circular routes. Many local guides detail circular options, and komoot offers several, such as the &amp;lt;a href=\\\"https://www.komoot.com/smarttour/e1294473914/hare-moss-and-big-wood-loop-from-dunhog-moss\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener\\\"&amp;gt;Hare Moss and Big Wood loop from Dunhog Moss&amp;lt;/a&amp;gt;, an easy 7.4 km path winding through varied scenery, or the &amp;lt;a href=\\\"https://www.komoot.com/smarttour/e1294104053/selkirk-bridge-and-linglie-bridge-loop-from-victoria-park-roxburghshire\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener\\\"&amp;gt;Selkirk Bridge and Linglie Bridge loop from Victoria Park&amp;lt;/a&amp;gt;, a 4.3 km trail along river valleys.\"},{\"question\":\"What do other hikers say about the easy trails in Ettrick And Yarrow?\",\"answer\":\"The easy trails in Ettrick And Yarrow are highly regarded by the komoot community, with an average rating of 4.5 stars from over 300 reviews. Hikers often praise the tranquil atmosphere, the diverse scenery of river valleys and woodlands, and the well-maintained paths that make for an enjoyable and accessible outdoor experience.\"},{\"question\":\"Are there any places to eat or drink near the easy hiking trails?\",\"answer\":\"While the region is known for its tranquil and remote feel, you can find amenities in nearby towns and villages. Selkirk, for instance, is a good base with options for cafes and pubs. Some estates, like Bowhill Country Estate, may also offer facilities. It's advisable to check opening times and availability, especially in more remote areas.\"},{\"question\":\"Is public transport available to access hiking trails in Ettrick And Yarrow?\",\"answer\":\"Public transport options in Ettrick And Yarrow can be limited due to its rural nature. Buses connect some of the larger towns like Selkirk, which can serve as a starting point for certain trails. However, for many of the more remote trailheads, personal transport is often the most convenient way to access them. Always check local bus schedules in advance.\"},{\"question\":\"Where can I find parking for easy hikes?\",\"answer\":\"Parking is generally available at or near trailheads, especially for popular routes and those starting from towns or estates. For example, trails around Selkirk, such as the &amp;lt;a href=\\\"https://www.komoot.com/smarttour/4087570\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener\\\"&amp;gt;Sir Walter Scott Statue – The Haining Estate loop from Selkirk&amp;lt;/a&amp;gt;, often have designated parking areas. It's always a good idea to check specific route information for parking details before you set out.\"}],\"page_title\":\"Easy hikes and walks around Ettrick And Yarrow\",\"page_description\":\"Exploring Ettrick And Yarrow on foot is a delightful way to connect with nature. Here are the top easy hikes and walks around Ettrick And Yarrow. \",\"centroid\":{\"lat\":55.47587946671404,\"lng\":-3.111838762602379},\"extent\":[{\"lat\":55.341467692543254,\"lng\":-3.3584529158975576},{\"lat\":55.592498381411495,\"lng\":-2.8249957071815146}],\"poor_quality\":false,\"share_url\":\"https://www.komoot.com/guide/3596813/easy-hikes-around-ettrick-and-yarrow\",\"changed_at\":\"2026-11-07T10:27:46.556Z\",\"visitors\":6728,\"rating_count\":675,\"rating_score\":4.549029350280762,\"difficulty\":\"EASY\",\"searchType\":\"within_radius\",\"_links\":{\"self\":{\"href\":\"https://api.komoot.de/v007/guides/3596813\"},\"ancestors\":{\"href\":\"https://api.komoot.de/v007/guides/3596813/ancestors/\"},\"elements\":{\"href\":\"https://api.komoot.de/v007/guides/3596813/elements/\"},\"smarttours\":{\"href\":\"https://api.komoot.de/v007/guides/3596813/smarttours/\"},\"discover_tours\":{\"href\":\"https://api.komoot.de/v007/guides/3596813/discover_tours/\"},\"highlights\":{\"href\":\"https://api.komoot.de/v007/guides/3596813/highlights/\"},\"siblings\":{\"href\":\"https://api.komoot.de/v007/guides/3596813/siblings/\"},\"cousins\":{\"href\":\"https://api.komoot.de/v007/guides/3596813/cousins/\"},\"subguides\":{\"href\":\"https://api.komoot.de/v007/guides/3596813/subguides/\"},\"map_image\":{\"href\":\"https://api.komoot.de/v007/regions/163434/map_image\"},\"tour_lines\":{\"h