explore the tranquil Ettrick Water and Yarrow Water valleys, as well as wild moorland. This area provides a chance to connect with nature amidst varied terrain.\\n  &amp;lt;/p&amp;gt;\\n\\n  &amp;lt;h2&amp;gt;Best jogging routes around Ettrick And Yarrow&amp;lt;/h2&amp;gt;\\n  &amp;lt;ul class=\\\"trail-highlights\\\"&amp;gt;\\n    &amp;lt;li&amp;gt;\\n      The most popular jogging route is &amp;lt;a href=\\\"https://www.komoot.com/smarttour/e1091520679/st-mary-s-loch-loop\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener\\\"&amp;gt;St Mary's Loch loop&amp;lt;/a&amp;gt;, a 7.4 miles (11.9 km) trail that takes about 1 hour 18 minutes to complete. This moderate route features mostly paved surfaces around the picturesque loch.\\n    &amp;lt;/li&amp;gt;\\n\\n    &amp;lt;li&amp;gt;\\n      Another top favourite among local runners is &amp;lt;a href=\\\"https://www.komoot.com/smarttour/e1091414902/grey-mare-s-tail-and-loch-skeen-trail\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener\\\"&amp;gt;Grey Mare's Tail and Loch Skeen Trail&amp;lt;/a&amp;gt;, a difficult 6.3 miles (10.2 km) path. This route involves a challenging climb alongside the spectacular 60-meter waterfall to the serene Loch Skeen.\\n    &amp;lt;/li&amp;gt;\\n\\n    &amp;lt;li&amp;gt;\\n      Local runners also love the &amp;lt;a href=\\\"https://www.komoot.com/smarttour/e1307758748/st-mary-s-loch-dun-rig-blackhouse-heights-loop-southern-uplands\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener\\\"&amp;gt;St Mary's Loch, Dun Rig & Blackhouse Heights loop — Southern Uplands&amp;lt;/a&amp;gt;, a 21.3 miles (34.3 km) trail leading through rolling hills and moorland, often completed in about 4 hours 4 minutes.\\n    &amp;lt;/li&amp;gt;\\n\\n    &amp;lt;li&amp;gt;\\n      Jogging around Ettrick And Yarrow is defined by river valleys, lochs, and rolling hills. The network of routes offers options for various ability levels, from easy paths to challenging climbs.\\n    &amp;lt;/li&amp;gt;\\n\\n    &amp;lt;li&amp;gt;\\n      The routes in Ettrick And Yarrow are highly rated by the komoot community with an average score of 4.8 stars from more than 10 reviews. More than 2000 runners have used komoot to explore Ettrick And Yarrow's varied terrain.\\n    &amp;lt;/li&amp;gt;\\n  &amp;lt;/ul&amp;gt;\\n&amp;lt;/div&amp;gt;\",\"sanitized_intro\":[\"Jogging around Ettrick And Yarrow offers diverse and scenic landscapes, characterized by beautiful hill and river scenery. The region features delightful river valleys, glistening lochs, extensive woodlands, and rolling hills. Runners can explore the tranquil Ettrick Water and Yarrow Water valleys, as well as wild moorland. This area provides a chance to connect with nature amidst varied terrain.\",\"Best jogging routes around Ettrick And Yarrow\",\"The most popular jogging route is St Mary&#39;s Loch loop, a 7.4 miles (11.9 km) trail that takes about 1 hour 18 minutes to complete. This moderate route features mostly paved surfaces around the picturesque loch.\",\"Another top favourite among local runners is Grey Mare&#39;s Tail and Loch Skeen Trail, a difficult 6.3 miles (10.2 km) path. This route involves a challenging climb alongside the spectacular 60-meter waterfall to the serene Loch Skeen.\",\"Local runners also love the St Mary&#39;s Loch, Dun Rig &amp; Blackhouse Heights loop — Southern Uplands, a 21.3 miles (34.3 km) trail leading through rolling hills and moorland, often completed in about 4 hours 4 minutes.\",\"Jogging around Ettrick And Yarrow is defined by river valleys, lochs, and rolling hills. The network of routes offers options for various ability levels, from easy paths to challenging climbs.\",\"The routes in Ettrick And Yarrow are highly rated by the komoot community with an average score of 4.8 stars from more than 10 reviews. More than 2000 runners have used komoot to explore Ettrick And Yarrow&#39;s varied terrain.\"],\"intro_plain\":\"Jogging around Ettrick And Yarrow offers diverse and scenic landscapes, characterized by beautiful hill and river scenery. The region features delightful river valleys, glistening lochs, extensive woodlands, and rolling hills. Runners can explore the tranquil Ettrick Water and Yarrow Water valleys, as well as wild moorland. This area provides a chance to connect with nature amidst varied terrain. Best jogging routes around Ettrick And Yarrow The most popular jogging route is St Mary's Loch loop, a 7.4 miles (11.9 km) trail that takes about 1 hour 18 minutes to complete. This moderate route features mostly paved surfaces around the picturesque loch. Another top favourite among local runners is Grey Mare's Tail and Loch Skeen Trail, a difficult 6.3 miles (10.2 km) path. This route involves a challenging climb alongside the spectacular 60-meter waterfall to the serene Loch Skeen. Local runners also love the St Mary's Loch, Dun Rig & Blackhouse Heights loop — Southern Uplands, a 21.3 miles (34.3 km) trail leading through rolling hills and moorland, often completed in about 4 hours 4 minutes. Jogging around Ettrick And Yarrow is defined by river valleys, lochs, and rolling hills. The network of routes offers options for various ability levels, from easy paths to challenging climbs. The routes in Ettrick And Yarrow are highly rated by the komoot community with an average score of 4.8 stars from more than 10 reviews. More than 2000 runners have used komoot to explore Ettrick And Yarrow's varied terrain.\",\"faq\":[{\"question\":\"How many running routes are available in Ettrick and Yarrow?\",\"answer\":\"There are over 160 running routes around Ettrick and Yarrow, offering a wide variety of options for different skill levels and preferences. You'll find everything from easy paths to challenging climbs.\"},{\"question\":\"What kind of terrain can I expect on the running trails in Ettrick and Yarrow?\",\"answer\":\"The region is characterized by diverse terrain, including delightful river valleys along the Ettrick Water and Yarrow Water, glistening lochs, extensive woodlands, and rolling hills. You can expect a mix of mostly paved surfaces around lochs, well-maintained paths, and more rugged, challenging trails in hilly and moorland areas.\"},{\"question\":\"Are there any easy running routes suitable for beginners or a relaxed jog?\",\"answer\":\"Yes, Ettrick and Yarrow offers several easy running routes. For instance, the &amp;lt;a href=\\\"https://www.komoot.com/smarttour/e1091520679/st-mary-s-loch-loop\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener\\\"&amp;gt;St Mary's Loch loop&amp;lt;/a&amp;gt; is a moderate 11.9 km trail with mostly paved surfaces, suitable for all skill levels. Additionally, the Ettrick Water South Route near Selkirk provides well-maintained paths with gentle inclines, perfect for a relaxed run. Bowhill Estate also features easy, leisurely tracks around its lochs and along the Yarrow Water.\"},{\"question\":\"Are there any challenging running routes for experienced runners?\",\"answer\":\"Absolutely. For those seeking a more strenuous run, the &amp;lt;a href=\\\"https://www.komoot.com/smarttour/e1091414902/grey-mare-s-tail-and-loch-skeen-trail\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener\\\"&amp;gt;Grey Mare's Tail and Loch Skeen Trail&amp;lt;/a&amp;gt; is a difficult 10.2 km path with significant elevation gain, climbing alongside a spectacular 60-meter waterfall. Another demanding option is the &amp;lt;a href=\\\"https://www.komoot.com/smarttour/e1307758748/st-mary-s-loch-dun-rig-blackhouse-heights-loop-southern-uplands\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener\\\"&amp;gt;St Mary's Loch, Dun Rig & Blackhouse Heights loop&amp;lt;/a&amp;gt;, a 34.3 km trail through rolling hills and moorland.\"},{\"question\":\"What natural features or landmarks can I see while running in Ettrick and Yarrow?\",\"answer\":\"The region boasts stunning natural features. You can run past the picturesque &amp;lt;a href=\\\"https://www.komoot.com/highlight/1073511\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener\\\"&amp;gt;St Mary's Loch&amp;lt;/a&amp;gt;, witness the dramatic &amp;lt;a href=\\\"https://www.komoot.com/highlight/4924314\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener\\\"&amp;gt;Grey Mare’s Tail Waterfall&amp;lt;/a&amp;gt;, and explore the serene Loch Skeen. The area also offers views of rolling hills like the 'Ettrick Horseshoe' and ancient woodlands at places like Bowhill Estate.\"},{\"question\":\"Are there any running routes that feature waterfalls?\",\"answer\":\"Yes, the &amp;lt;a href=\\\"https://www.komoot.com/smarttour/e1091414902/grey-mare-s-tail-and-loch-skeen-trail\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener\\\"&amp;gt;Grey Mare's Tail and Loch Skeen Trail&amp;lt;/a&amp;gt; is an excellent choice. This challenging route takes you alongside the spectacular 60-meter &amp;lt;a href=\\\"https://www.komoot.com/highlight/4924314\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener\\\"&amp;gt;Grey Mare’s Tail Waterfall&amp;lt;/a&amp;gt;, one of Scotland's finest, before climbing to the beautiful Loch Skeen.\"},{\"question\":\"Are the running routes in Ettrick and Yarrow suitable for families?\",\"answer\":\"Many routes in Ettrick and Yarrow can be adapted for family-friendly jogs, especially the easier, flatter sections. The &amp;lt;a href=\\\"https://www.komoot.com/smarttour/e1091520679/st-mary-s-loch-loop\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener\\\"&amp;gt;St Mary's Loch loop&amp;lt;/a&amp;gt;, with its mostly paved surfaces, is a good option. Circular walks around Ettrickbridge and Yarrowford, such as the Ettrickbridge Village Walk, are also generally easy and can be enjoyed by families.\"},{\"question\":\"Can I bring my dog on the running trails in Ettrick and Yarrow?\",\"answer\":\"Generally, dogs are welcome on many of the running trails in Ettrick and Yarrow. However, it's always advisable to keep dogs on a lead, especially in areas with livestock or ground-nesting birds, and to follow the Scottish Outdoor Access Code. Always check specific route details or local signage for any restrictions.\"},{\"question\":\"Are there circular running routes available in the region?\",\"answer\":\"Yes, Ettrick and Yarrow offers several circular running routes. The &amp;lt;a href=\\\"https://www.komoot.com/smarttour/e1091520679/st-mary-s-loch-loop\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener\\\"&amp;gt;St Mary's Loch loop&amp;lt;/a&amp;gt; is a popular circular option. Additionally, many of the circular walks around Ettrickbridge and Yarrowford can be adapted for jogging, providing varying distances and views.\"},{\"question\":\"What do other runners say about the trails in Ettrick and Yarrow?\",\"answer\":\"The running routes in Ettrick and Yarrow are highly rated by the komoot community, with an average score of 4.8 stars from more than 10 reviews. Runners often praise the tranquil scenery, diverse landscapes, and the opportunity to connect with nature in this peaceful and largely undiscovered area.\"},{\"question\":\"Is there parking available near the running routes?\",\"answer\":\"Parking is generally available at key access points for many popular routes. For example, there are parking facilities near St Mary's Loch and the Grey Mare's Tail Waterfall. It's recommended to check specific route information for designated parking areas before you go.\"},{\"question\":\"What is the best time of year to go running in Ettrick and Yarrow?\",\"answer\":\"Ettrick and Yarrow offers beautiful running opportunities year-round. Spring and autumn provide pleasant temperatures and stunning seasonal colours. Summer is ideal for longer runs, while winter can offer crisp, clear days, though some higher or more remote trails may require more caution due to weather conditions. Always check local weather forecasts before heading out.\"}],\"page_title\":\"The best running trails around Ettrick And Yarrow\",\"page_description\":\"Discover the best running trails around Ettrick And Yarrow: See interactive maps and full route profiles of the best places to run—and browse other runners' photos and tips!\",\"centroid\":{\"lat\":55.47587946671404,\"lng\":-3.111838762602379},\"extent\":[{\"lat\":55.341467692543254,\"lng\":-3.3584529158975576},{\"lat\":55.592498381411495,\"lng\":-2.8249957071815146}],\"poor_quality\":false,\"share_url\":\"https://www.komoot.com/guide/2756305/running-trails-around-ettrick-and-yarrow\",\"changed_at\":\"2026-11-08T12:19:10.187Z\",\"visitors\":2639,\"rating_count\":29,\"rating_score\":4.653846263885498,\"searchType\":\"within_radius\",\"_links\":{\"self\":{\"href\":\"https://api.komoot.de/v007/guides/2756305\"},\"ancestors\":{\"href\":\"https://api.komoot.de/v007/guides/2756305/ancestors/\"},\"elements\":{\"href\":\"https://api.komoot.de/v007/guides/2756305/elements/\"},\"smarttours\":{\"href\":\"https://api.komoot.de/v007/guides/2756305/smarttours/\"},\"discover_tours\":{\"href\":\"https://api.komoot.de/v007/guides/2756305/discover_tours/\"},\"highlights\":{\"href\":\"https://api.komoot.de/v007/guides/2756305/highlights/\"},\"siblings\":{\"href\":\"https://api.komoot.de/v007/guides/2756305/siblings/\"},\"cousins\":{\"href\":\"https://api.komoot.de/v007/guides/2756305/cousins/\"},\"subguides\":{\"href\":\"https://api.komoot.de/v007/guides/2756305/subguides/\"},\"map_image\":{\"href\":\"https://api.komoot.de/v007/regions/163434/map_image\"},\"tour_lines\":{\"href\":\"https://api.komoot.de/v007/guides/2756305/tour_lines/\"},\"saved\":{\"href\":\"https://api.komoot.de/v007/guides/2756305/saved/{username}\",\"templated\":true},\"cover_image\":{\"href\":\"https://api.komoot.de/v007/guides/2756305/cover_image\"},\"featured\":{\"href\":\"https://www.komoot.com/webapi/v007/guides/2756305/featured/\"},\"seo_guides\":{\"href\":\"https://www.komoot.com/webapi/v007/guides/2756305/seo_guides/\"},\"collections\":{\"href\":\"https://api.komoot.de/v007/guides/2756305/collections/\"},\"weather\":{\"href\":\"https://weather-along-tour-api.komoot.de/v1/weather/55.475879,-3.111839\"}},\"_meta\":{\"_isLoaded\":true},\"_embedded\":{\"cover_image\